# Shadowfetch core system packages
# These are required regardless of the variant being built.

# Kernel and bootloader
linux-image-amd64
linux-headers-amd64
firmware-linux
firmware-linux-nonfree
firmware-misc-nonfree
firmware-iwlwifi
firmware-realtek
firmware-atheros
firmware-brcm80211

# --- audio firmware. Added 2026-07-26 ------------------------------------
# firmware-sof-signed is the gap that mattered. Sound Open Firmware drives
# the audio DSP on essentially every Intel laptop from Tiger Lake onward
# (2019+). Without it those machines have NO SOUND AT ALL - not quiet, not
# wrong output, nothing - and the cause is invisible: the driver loads and
# then fails to fetch the DSP blob.
#
# alsa-ucm-conf carries the Use Case Manager profiles that route those
# codecs correctly; SOF without UCM gets you a card that exists and still
# plays nothing through the speakers.
#
# firmware-cirrus covers the Cirrus Logic smart amps in newer ThinkPads and
# XPS machines.
#
# Roughly 54 MB uncompressed, about 20-30 MB after squashfs compression
# (measured ratio 11.34 GiB -> 3.96 GiB). Headroom before the FAT32 4 GiB
# per-file limit was 41 MiB, so this fits - but only just. Anything further
# needs something removed first; check `ls -la filesystem.squashfs` after
# a build before adding more.
firmware-sof-signed
alsa-ucm-conf
firmware-cirrus
intel-microcode
amd64-microcode
grub-efi-amd64
grub-pc-bin
shim-signed
efibootmgr

# Live system essentials
live-boot
live-config
live-config-systemd
live-tools

# syslinux-utils provides isohybrid (lb_binary_iso runs it inside the chroot;
# Debian testing split isohybrid out of syslinux into syslinux-utils)
syslinux-utils

